n-2"], "prerequisites": [], "modes": [{"label": "Focus on the key idea", "text": "Connect percentages to fractions and decimals. Fifty percent is 50/100, which equals one half and 0.5."}], "quickCheck": {"prompt": "Which decimal equals 50 percent?", "options": ["50.0", "0.5"], "correctIndex": 1, "explanation": "0.5. A percentage can be written as a fraction over 100 or as a decimal. Fifty percent is 50/100, which equals one half and 0.5."}}}, {"title": "Find a percentage", "block_type": "relationships", "sequence": 2, "objective": "Find a simple percentage of a quantity", "required": true, "content": {"body": "Ten percent is one tenth of a quantity. Divide the quantity by ten, so ten percent of 80 is 8.", "competencyKeys": ["foundation-3"], "prerequisites": [], "modes": [{"label": "Focus on the key idea", "text": "Find a simple percentage of a quantity. Divide the quantity by ten, so ten percent of 80 is 8."}], "quickCheck": {"prompt": "What is ten percent of 80?", "options": ["8", "10"], "correctIndex": 0, "explanation": "8. Ten percent is one tenth of a quantity. Divide the quantity by ten, so ten percent of 80 is 8."}}}, {"title": "Identify the base", "block_type": "relationships", "sequence": 3, "objective": "Identify the whole used in a percentage", "required": true, "content": {"body": "A percentage is always taken relative to a whole or base. If 20 of 50 learners walk to school, the whole is the 50 learners, not the 20 who walk.", "competencyKeys": ["foundation-4"], "prerequisites": [], "modes": [{"label": "Focus on the key idea", "text": "Identify the whole used in a percentage. If 20 of 50 learners walk to school, the whole is the 50 learners, not the 20 who walk."}], "quickCheck": {"prompt": "Twenty of fifty learners walk to school. What is the reference whole?", "options": ["Twenty learners", "Fifty learners"], "correctIndex": 1, "explanation": "Fifty learners. A percentage is always taken relative to a whole or base. If 20 of 50 learners walk to school, 